Implement a rough engineering model to estimate traffic redistribution after one or multiple serving cells go down.

Inputs
------
1. Coverage data
   - Coordinates
   - RSRP of every cell at every coordinate

2. Historical statistics
   - Average RRC connections of each cell
   - Average PRB utilization of each cell

3. GIS data
   - Population density
   - OSM land-use / feature labels
     (residential, commercial, highway, industrial, farmland, forest, etc.)

4. Target outage cells

-------------------------------------------------------

Step 1. Estimate pre-outage demand distribution.

For each outage cell:

Compute a demand score for every coordinate covered by the cell:

DemandScore =
PopulationDensity
× OSMWeight
× exp((RSRP+120)/10)

Normalize all demand scores so that they sum to 1.

Distribute the historical RRC of the outage cell to every coordinate according to the normalized demand score.

-------------------------------------------------------

Step 2. Redistribute traffic.

For every coordinate:

Find all remaining cells with RSRP > -105 dBm.

If no candidate exists:
    classify as Coverage Hole.

Otherwise compute

Softmax(RSRP)

over all candidate cells.

Distribute the coordinate RRC proportionally according to the softmax weights.

-------------------------------------------------------

Step 3. Estimate PRB increase.

For every cell:

Compute

ResourcePerConnection =
HistoricalPRB / HistoricalRRC

Estimate

AdditionalPRB =
ResourcePerConnection × redistributed RRC

Update

NewPRB =
HistoricalPRB + AdditionalPRB

-------------------------------------------------------

Step 4. Classify every coordinate.

Coverage Hole:
    no candidate cell

Weak Coverage:
    strongest backup RSRP between -115 and -105 dBm

Capacity Limited:
    strongest backup exists
    but its estimated PRB > 90%

Healthy:
    backup RSRP > -105 dBm
    estimated PRB <= 90%

-------------------------------------------------------

Step 5. Aggregate results.

Group neighbouring coordinates into contiguous regions.

Summarize each region by

- dominant OSM feature
- average population density
- number of coordinates
- percentage Healthy
- percentage Weak Coverage
- percentage Capacity Limited
- percentage Coverage Hole

Generate visualizations and statistics for every region.
